WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.801
When the Cold War ended,

2
00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:04.147
two scholars made bold predictions.

3
00:00:04.147 --> 00:00:06.341
They couldn't both be right.

4
00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:07.607
In 1989,

5
00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:10.911
Fukuyama argued liberal democracy had

6
00:00:10.911 --> 00:00:13.412
won the battle of ideas.

7
00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:14.335
In 1993,

8
00:00:14.335 --> 00:00:18.146
Huntington predicted conflict along cultural

9
00:00:18.146 --> 00:00:19.226
lines.

10
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:20.871
From bipolar,

11
00:00:20.871 --> 00:00:23.203
to a unipolar moment after

12
00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:26.096
1991, to an emerging multipolar

13
00:00:26.096 --> 00:00:27.106
order.

14
00:00:27.442 --> 00:00:30.776
India's answer has been multi-alignment.

15
00:00:30.776 --> 00:00:32.027
Partners with many,

16
00:00:32.027 --> 00:00:33.609
allied with none.

17
00:00:34.283 --> 00:00:35.509
Your turn.

18
00:00:35.509 --> 00:00:37.365
Whose argument?
